# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# This is load bearing, not hygiene. Git for Windows installs with
# core.autocrlf=true by default and the CI runner image keeps that
# default, so without this file a Windows checkout rewrites every .go
# file with CRLF — and `gofmt -l` lists a CRLF file as unformatted.
# `fmt` is the first prerequisite of `make ci`, so the Windows job would
# be red at step one, on files nobody had touched.
#
# It also keeps the citation guard and the pattern manifest reading
# byte-identical line endings on all three platforms, which is one less
# way for a guard to disagree with itself depending on where it ran.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries are never line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
